{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1159365-help-me-flesh-out-my-mta-setting","id":1159365,"title":"Help me flesh out my MtA setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-16T01:29:15-08:00","id":1159365,"title":"Help me flesh out my MtA setting","content":"After over a year I'm back to storytelling, with my wife as the only player. SHe has awesome character and I wanted to continue what we started but I lost my whole campaign notes ;( THerefore, we decided to restart in the same setting with new storyline. I re-created the sketch of the setting and now I'm trying to flesh it up with both mundane and magical stuff. What I need the most are story seeds and mysteries for my player to get involved into different things happening. So, anyone willing to help?<br /> <br /> <u>Somewhere in Magick</u><br /> Setting and chronicle sketch<br /> <b>Basic Information</b><br /><br /> <b>Game System: </b>Mage: the Awakening 2ed<br /> <b>Number of players</b>: 1<br /> <b>Game Limits: </b> Tier One (No Orders, no rotes at the beginning, PC is the only awakened in the area)<br /> <b>Theme</b>: Discovery<br /> <b>Mood</b>: Shamanistic-Criminal<br /> <b>Focus on</b>: Role-Play, relationships with NPC, slow discovery of the magical side of the area<br /> <b>Magic filter</b>: Native American Shamanism <b>Very short plot summary</b><br /><br /> Under/Next to the city of Somewhere there are ruins. Ruins actually. They are from <i>The Times Before</i> and are extremely dangerous. Once, for the fact that they are ancient magical ruins, two because of the artefact that is resting there. The artefact, known in more recent times as the Pandora\u2019s Box could be traced over many continents and many catastrophic events over the centuries. No one knows how it came to America nor how it came to this specific location. Its last guardian died during the Namless War (1899-1901). While dying he cast a spell to protect the temple. The spell, that used all his remaining lifeforce as a fuel, hid the temple from the unwanted eyes. The side effect leaked also at the city of Somewhere. It was not so much hidden as occluded. No important event ever happened there, no big company every took interest in the place, even internet and telecom data seem to be omitting the place. However, now, after over a century since the death of the guardian, the spell starts to weaken, and some people take newly revived interest in the city. As if that wasn\u2019t enough on its own, since magic protecting Pandora\u2019s Box is weakening the artefact starts leaking its foul, abyss-tainted mana into the area surrounding the city. <b>Mortal setting overview</b><br /><br /> Somewhere is a small American town, in the middle of Nowhere county, deep on the NE of USA in the Maine state. The city counts approx. 12 000 permanent inhabitants and borders an Passquemada Indians reservation. The indian village in the reservation accounts for next 600-700 souls.<br /> The city itself is almost nothing out of ordinary, with all the basic institutions and facilities in place. It feels somewhat as if it stopped in late 1990s/2000s, with even the internet not always working properly. The exceptions from what you could expect in a small town are as follows:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>There are no chain-stores or chain-restaurants. Everything in Somewhere is locally owned</li> <li>There is no hospital in the city. For many years there was no doctor as well, recently the situation changed for better and the hospital is being built, but years must pass before it will be ready</li> </ol>Within last 2-3 years city experienced large inflow of money and newcomers because of the ACME Inc. It\u2019s the first corporation that ever appeared in the city. They obtained a license for wood harvesting from the city council and started intensive forest-cutting near to the city. Moreover, the corporation brought some of their own people and gave well-paid jobs to several people in the city. They also hire anyone who wants to work as a wood-cutter which results in many suspicious individuals flocking to the city to work in well-paid (over $25/h) but dangerous job.<br /> The inflow of no-always-well-behaved newcomers\u2019 putts high pressure on local police officer - the close to retirement sheriff John Johnson (who is also a brother of a mayor) as they overuse alcohol, get into fights, and so on. <b>Atlantean Orders presence</b><br /><br /> None. Actually Orders are probably blissfully unaware of the existence of the place. <b>Player Character</b><br /><br /> Sally Brown the Raven Shaman (Thyrsus Arcana: Life 3, Death 3, Spirit 1, Gnosis 2) \u2013 Passquemada indian by birth, M.D. by profession. Smart, hard-working girl who managed to run away from Somewhere to Boston where she graduated from medical college and worked for some years for Boston Police Dpt. After seeing some things-that-should-not-be-seen she started seeing Mysteries everywhere. What is worse some people started following her at the same time. Running away from them Sally quit work in Boston Police, took car and drove North on the verge of extensive forests in Maine, planning to lose whoever is following her there and go back to her hometown on foot. Things went not exactly as planned and resulted in couple of weeks trek instead of 3 days and awakening of the PC. When she returned to her village her grandma, who was a shaman of the village, officially made her new shaman. Not really feeling ready to go back and face whatever happened in Boston Sally settled down on the verge of Somewhere and opened, much needed, private medical practice, while serving as a new shaman of the Passquemada tribe. <b>The Stories</b><br /><br /> As the abyss-tained mana leaks from the artefact more and more strange and unnatural events will be happening around the city. It is only a matter of time before some Awakened will notice that. But before that happens I want to keep power-level relatively low and use other threats and antagonists that awakened. Looking at my PC\u2019s profile the dead should appear heavily, but as for now I\u2019ll gladly welcome any idea that can fit in the tone of the setting. It should be something low-key, does not have to be terribly powerful, and very local. I\u2019m trying to avoid things that bring more meta-setting like Abyss intruders, Order-related thingies, SoT or Banishers, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T08:24:39-08:00","id":1159423,"title":"","content":"Local Cult of the Red Word could work pretty well with the Native American folklore. Chenoo cannibal spirits in the area could be at war with incursions of corrupted cannibal spirits or maybe just one that is the leader of the Cult in the area.<br /> <br /> The Artifact could be an Abyssal Verge to the Prince of 100,000 Leaves, for instance. Maybe as the taint spreads, more and more tribal writings are being over-written by the Leaves and the Cult is trying to acquire them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-16-2017, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T11:36:10-08:00","id":1159936,"title":"","content":"With the outside world re-discovering your city along with big business will come outside crime, especially with an influx of &quot;not-always-well-behaved-newcomers&quot;. Given her role as the town's only doctor and mentioned previous work with the police Sally Brown will have a front row seat to much of it, possibly even working as the city's Medical Examiner.<br /> <br /> \u200bGiven their long term isolation, neighboring native culture and mysterious ruins there are going to be secret societies in your city, even if they never number more than a dozen people at a time or just one extended family. They may be small but they will be deeply entrenched and who knows what shenanigans they may be up to.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe ruins predate the arrival of Pandora's Box, so do they have guardians of their own? Over the years have any of the locals trespassed, dug down into tunnels when laying infrastructure or plowing fields and what where the consequences? How did the city's likely Protestant founders explain the ruins presence, did they write off reports as pagan myth? What did the local natives think of them, they do predate the spell that hid them for so long and should have an oral history relating to the ruins.<br /> <br /> \u200bWith three points in Death ghosts are going to be a big thing in your chronicle and the city might have a lot of them, given its long isolation many may be there because they never really thought of moving on to a place 'outside'. They don't all have to be malignant, some might even be helpful to those who watch their step, like the old man who still spends the morning hours in that rocker out front of the local grocer telling stories about the town when he was young.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T02:57:31-08:00","id":1160462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1159365-help-me-flesh-out-my-mta-setting?p=1159936#post1159936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the outside world re-discovering your city along with big business will come outside crime, especially with an influx of &quot;not-always-well-behaved-newcomers&quot;. Given her role as the town's only doctor and mentioned previous work with the police Sally Brown will have a front row seat to much of it, possibly even working as the city's Medical Examiner.</div> </div> </div> </div>yup. Already included.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1159365-help-me-flesh-out-my-mta-setting?p=1159936#post1159936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given their long term isolation, neighboring native culture and mysterious ruins there are going to be secret societies in your city, even if they never number more than a dozen people at a time or just one extended family. They may be small but they will be deeply entrenched and who knows what shenanigans they may be up to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a cool idea I never thought about. Somehow I got fixated on Mystery Society = big mysterious cult. I'm incorporating it.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1159365-help-me-flesh-out-my-mta-setting?p=1159936#post1159936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ruins predate the arrival of Pandora's Box, so do they have guardians of their own? Over the years have any of the locals trespassed, dug down into tunnels when laying infrastructure or plowing fields and what where the consequences? How did the city's likely Protestant founders explain the ruins presence, did they write off reports as pagan myth? What did the local natives think of them, they do predate the spell that hid them for so long and should have an oral history relating to the ruins.</div> </div> </div> </div>AWESOME! Those are exactly the questions I needed to flesh the whole things out. YOu opened a new dimension to my prep. Thanks man!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}